      "message": "This will bind to the local |uniformValue|, which goes out of scope.  We prolly want something like\n\n  fUniforms.push_back(std::make_tuple(uniformName-\u003etoString(),\n                                      VectorValue()));\n  this-\u003ebind(abuilder, (*jprop)[\"v\"], std::get\u003c1\u003e(fUniforms.back()));\n  \nBut that\u0027s bad, because bind() grabs the address of the target VectorValue, which may change if fUniforms reallocates as it grows.\n\nSo we either need two passes or we could allocate VectorValues dynamically:\n\n  std::vector\u003cstd::tuple\u003cSkString, std::unique_ptr\u003cVectorValue\u003e\u003e\u003e fUniforms;\n  \n  ..\n  fUniforms.push_back(std::make_tuple(uniformName-\u003etoString(),\n                                      std::make_unique\u003cVectorValue\u003e()));\n  this-\u003ebind(abuilder, (*jprop)[\"v\"], std::get\u003c1\u003e(fUniforms.back()).get());",
